{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "Sara has babysat her younger cousins before, but tonight is her first real paid job."
    },
    {
      "text": "The Alvarez family lives just two houses down, and their son David is five years old."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sara has promised herself she won't panic, no matter what happens."
    },
    {
      "text": "Mrs. Alvarez leaves a long list of instructions taped to the fridge before rushing out the door."
    },
    {
      "text": "Everything goes smoothly until bedtime arrives and David flatly refuses to sleep."
    },
    {
      "text": "He wants three more stories, then a glass of water."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then he wants the hallway light left on a specific way."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sara has read the same book twice already, and her voice is getting hoarse."
    },
    {
      "text": "She remembers something her own babysitter used to do years ago."
    },
    {
      "text": "If David helps her build a blanket fort first, he might finally feel tired enough to sleep."
    },
    {
      "text": "It's a small risk, since fort-building usually makes kids more awake, not less."
    },
    {
      "text": "Surprisingly, it works."
    },
    {
      "text": "David arranges the pillows with total concentration, discussing exactly where each cushion should go."
    },
    {
      "text": "He insists the biggest pillow must go at the very top, like a roof."
    },
    {
      "text": "By the time the fort is finished, he's yawning between sentences without even noticing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sara tucks him inside the small fort instead of his usual bed, and he's asleep within minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "She checks on him twice before his parents return, just to be sure."
    },
    {
      "text": "When Mrs. Alvarez gets home, she finds Sara quietly reading on the couch."
    },
    {
      "text": "The house is completely, wonderfully quiet."
    },
    {
      "text": "\"How did you manage that?\" Mrs. Alvarez whispers, peeking into David's room."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sara just smiles and says some things are better explained tomorrow."
    }
  ],
